From 1b10e1f60cf7436ff815d27f667e16988d8a7a70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ebg-ant <296364998+ebg-ant@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 22:40:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] test: the chaos lab's placement rules, walks about desks,
 and replays that say what was refused

Where Arbor puts a window is judged at the step of the move: placed-out-of-reach, placed-partly-out,
placed-mostly-out, grown-while-hanging, docked-partly-out, left-its-place, moved-for-nothing.
New: windows-silent, replay --go-on with REFUSED lines, hunt --pass, and the walks ARBOR_CHAOS_DESKS,
WINDOWS_FIRST, TWO_DISPLAYS and HOLDS. The squeezed window its user nudged is a plain regression test:
the fault is mended.
